1.  If you read a scroll while hallucinating, the words you actually read will
be a randomly chosen scroll, since what you see may not actually be what is
there.  

2.  If you are hallucinating, you will not be able to completely identify 
things you pick up.  You would be able (by touch) to identify an item as a
potion, scroll, etc., but descriptions like color will be wrong.  Maybe the
colors would even change every time you looked at your inventory (unless you
already had the item before you started hallucinating, in which case you would
remember the correct description for the item at that slot).

3.  Add a smell command, or something like it, to approximately determine the
fitness of meat (fresh, rotten, tainted, and maybe degrees in between, so that
while you might not be able to positively determine its condition, at least you
could get an idea).

4.  Allow the player to pick up tiny monsters (newts, lizards, etc.) and simply
swallow them--a guaranteed source of food, and a quick kill too (and more fun). 
Grid bugs could be included, but they would zap you as you swallowed them and 
cause some damage.  Some others might take similar damage from you. 

5.  Allow the player to pick up and move pets (if they are small enough) to get
them out of the way.  And add a pet (as in rub or pat) command to use when
training pets.

I guess that's all... see what you think of them (and suggest modifications to
them if you have any.
